\ Focused fixture for the row-variable quotation-parameter consumer shape:
\ take-while runs `while` on its predicate/body quotation parameters inside a
\ `[ ... ] dip`, then shuffles the consumed span across the bounded row
\ (`2 pick-n`, `-rot> #slice`). The preserved-bounded-row layout keeps the
\ threaded scanner/start values live above the row, so the body compiles to
\ native C under runtime-image AOT and matches the interpreter.
use "scanner" ;

\ partial consumption: stop at the first space.
"hello world" <scanner> [ " " = not ] take-while
swap drop print-line

\ full consumption: predicate true for every char.
"12345" <scanner> [ " " = not ] take-while
swap drop print-line
